# ==============================
# ABOUT
# ==============================

msgid "about_title"
msgstr "Grimoria"

msgid "about_text"
msgstr ""
"Grimoria for KOReader\n"
"═══════════════════════════════\n"
"\n"
"WHAT IT DOES\n"
"Sends the actual text of the book you are reading to an AI, once,\n"
"and builds a reference index from it: characters, locations,\n"
"themes, a timeline, and any real historical figures mentioned.\n"
"\n"
"WHAT MAKES IT DIFFERENT\n"
"Every entry is tagged with the chapter it belongs to. Anything you\n"
"have not read yet is hidden on the device itself — no second\n"
"request, no extra cost. The index opens up as you read.\n"
"\n"
"That includes hidden identities: if a character appears under two\n"
"names, the two cards stay unconnected until the chapter where the\n"
"book itself connects them.\n"
"\n"
"═══════════════════════════════\n"
"\n"
"FEATURES:\n"
"\n"
"Characters\n"
"• Description, role, occupation\n"
"• Search by name\n"
"• Your own notes, per character\n"
"• Filtered to the chapter you have reached\n"
"\n"
"Timeline\n"
"• Key events in order\n"
"• Who was involved in each\n"
"\n"
"Historical figures\n"
"• Real people mentioned in the book\n"
"• Biography and context\n"
"\n"
"Locations, themes, summary\n"
"• All filtered by reading progress\n"
"\n"
"Storage\n"
"• Internet needed only for the first analysis\n"
"• Fully offline afterwards\n"
"• Stored per book\n"
"• Keeps several analyses, switch between them freely\n"
"\n"
"═══════════════════════════════\n"
"\n"
"GETTING STARTED:\n"
"\n"
"1. Set an API key\n"
"Menu → Grimoria → AI Settings\n"
"\n"
"2. Analyse\n"
"Menu → Grimoria → Analyze with AI\n"
"(A novel takes a few minutes. The device is kept awake\n"
"throughout, and you can tap the screen to cancel.)\n"
"\n"
"3. Read on!\n"
"The Grimoria expands by itself, chapter by chapter.\n"
"\n"
"═══════════════════════════════\n"
"\n"
"TIPS:\n"
"\n"
"• The AI writes in the language of the book itself\n"
"• Each book is analysed once\n"
"• Notes are saved per book\n"
"• After changing language, reopen the book\n"
"\n"
"═══════════════════════════════\n"
"\n"
"Happy reading!"

